    11	
    12	# Session lifecycle and worktree boundaries
    13	
    14	## Problem
    15	
    16	Before the v0.5.0 worktree-first redesign, session writes were ambiguous: session
    17	notes, project memory drafts, and mistake files could land in either the main tree
    18	or a worktree depending on which path the agent constructed. This produced two
    19	documented failure modes:
    20	
    21	- **Concurrent-session corruption.** Without per-session worktrees, two sessions
    22	  working in the same main tree produced overlapping diffs. The manager could not
    23	  tell which file changes belonged to which session, and legitimate work was
    24	  reverted as scope creep at review.
    25	- **Main-tree vs. worktree write-path ambiguity.** The `git/SKILL.md` rule at
    26	  line 33 formerly said "use the main-tree absolute path" unconditionally. A
    27	  worktree-aware agent following that rule would write session artifacts into the
    28	  main tree rather than the worktree, leaving the worktree branch empty and
    29	  producing a PR diff missing the session memory. The inverse failure
    30	  (`codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md`) produced the opposite
    31	  problem — all writes inside the worktree, including transcript paths that live
    32	  in `~/.claude/projects/` and are outside both trees.
    33	- **Session directory placement uncertainty.** Without a canonical rule for where
    34	  the session directory (`sessions/{date}-{session-id}/`) is rooted, agents had to
    35	  guess. Guesses diverged.
    36	
    37	The root cause was that no single rule captured "where does the write go when a
    38	worktree exists?" and "where does it go when one does not?"
    39	
    40	## Approach
    41	
    42	The v0.5.0 worktree-first model resolves the ambiguity with a single canonical
    43	decision made at Configuration Step 1 before any loop work begins.
    44	
    45	**Worktree creation precedes session.json init (D-1).** Row 5.5 of the
    46	Configuration Step 1 table in `orchestration/SKILL.md` creates the per-session
    47	worktree via `git/SKILL.md § P2` and stamps `session.json.git.worktreePath` and
    48	`session.json.git.branch` before row 6 (session.json full stamp) runs. Branch
    49	naming follows the convention: `chore/session-{date}-{ssid-short}` (e.g.,
    50	`chore/session-2026-05-24-45388fa9`), where `{ssid-short}` is the first 8
    51	characters of `$CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`. The branch name satisfies the
    52	`git/conventions.md` shape regex and the 3-50 character length constraint (27
    53	characters).
    54	
    55	**`worktreePath` is the absolute write-root (D-2).** The qualified rule in
    56	`git/SKILL.md` Memory Access Matrix and Constraints reads: "Use
    57	`session.json.git.worktreePath` as the absolute root when set; fall back to the
    58	main tree absolute path when `worktreePath` is null (direct mode)." Transcript
    59	paths (`session.json.transcriptPath`) live in `~/.claude/projects/` — outside
    60	both trees — and are never redirected.
    61	
    62	**Per-iteration session-memory commit cadence (D-4).** After each MEMORIZATION
    63	sub-phase completes, the manager commits the iteration's session-memory deltas to
    64	the worktree branch via `git -C "$worktreePath" commit`. Subject:
    65	`chore(session): record {loop} iter{n} memory`. This ensures session memory
    66	survives mid-session abort before Wrap-up runs — `git worktree remove` (Procedure
    67	P5) discards uncommitted state; committed state survives.
    68	
    69	**Direct-mode opt-out retained (D-5).** Row 5.5 is guarded: when
    70	`settings.git.workflow.mode == "direct"`, the row is skipped entirely — no
    71	worktree is created, `session.json.git.worktreePath` stays `null`, and
    72	`git.branch` is stamped from the current HEAD in row 6. Direct mode is the
    73	documented escape hatch for emergency hotfixes (where the PR lifecycle overhead is
    74	unacceptable) and pure-read sessions (no shippable artifact). Outside these two
    75	situations the default is `worktree-pr`.
    76	
    77	## Surfaces
    78	
    79	The worktree-first model is distributed across nine edited surfaces in the skill
    80	tree and session template:
    81	
    82	| Surface | What it carries |
    83	|---|---|
    84	| `orchestration/SKILL.md` Step 1 rows 5/5.5/6 | Row 5.5 definition: P2 invocation, idempotency 3-state machine, direct-mode guard, branch naming, `worktreePath` stamp order. Row 6: `git.branch` + `git.worktreePath` stamp source. Row 5.5 footnote: direct-mode opt-out prose (LOCK #5). Smoke-test gate prose. |
    85	| `orchestration/SKILL.md` Step 1 — smoke-test gate | Post-merge verification: `jq -r '.git.branch'` matches `^chore/session-[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}-[a-f0-9]{8}$`; `jq -r '.git.worktreePath'` returns non-null for `worktree-pr` sessions. |
    86	| `git/SKILL.md` Memory Access Matrix | Critical rule (last row): qualified write-path rule — `session.json.git.worktreePath` as absolute root when set; main-tree fallback when null; transcript paths outside both trees. |
    87	| `git/SKILL.md` § P2 — Create worktree | P2 is invoked from Configuration row 5.5, not from Execution start. Steps for sync, re-verify, create, install, pass path. |
    88	| `git/SKILL.md` § Constraints + Output paths | Constraint: "MUST root session notes and mistakes at `session.json.git.worktreePath` when set." Output paths table: session notes/mistakes row reflects worktree-first vs direct-mode distinction. |
    89	| Five workflow phase docs (`orchestration/workflow/`) | `execution.md`, `ideation.md`, `planning.md`, `preparation.md`, `wrap-up.md` each carry the per-iter session-memory commit cadence (D-4): heredoc commit subject + `AI-Provenance-Record:` trailer + direct-mode opt-out note. |
    90	| `delegation/SKILL.md` | Main-tree boilerplate corrected — delegation prompts reference `session.json.git.worktreePath` rather than a main-tree-absolute path. |
    91	| `orchestration/templates/session.template.json` | `git.worktreePath` and `git.branch` fields present in the template; `git.worktreePath` initializes to `null` (stamped by row 5.5 at runtime). |
    92	| `preparation/SKILL.md` | Narrow exception extension: executor commits on the worktree branch via `git -C "$worktreePath"` even for promote-now skills (the exception that applies within Preparation). |
    93	
    94	## Validation
    95	
    96	The model is checked at two levels:
    97	
    98	**Smoke-test gate (post-merge check).** After the feature merges to `develop`,
    99	every new `worktree-pr` session must satisfy both of the following checks at
   100	Memorization phase:
   101	
   102	```
   103	# Branch name matches the canonical shape regex
   104	jq -r '.git.branch' .gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/<latest>/session.json
   105	# Expected: ^chore/session-[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}-[a-f0-9]{8}$
   106	
   107	# worktreePath is non-null for worktree-pr sessions
   108	jq -r '.git.worktreePath' .gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/<latest>/session.json
   109	# Expected: a non-null absolute path
   110	```
   111	
   112	A null `worktreePath` on a `worktree-pr` session indicates row 5.5 was skipped
   113	or P2 failed without surfacing an error.
   114	
   115	**Session writes landing under `worktreePath`.** For any `worktree-pr` session,
   116	verify that `sessions/{date}-{session-id}/` is rooted inside the worktree, not
   117	in the main tree. Cross-check: `git -C "$worktreePath" log --oneline` should show
   118	`chore(session): record * iter* memory` commits appearing on the worktree branch.
   119	
   120	**Direct-mode consistency check.** When `settings.git.workflow.mode == "direct"`,
   121	`session.json.git.worktreePath` must be `null` and `git.branch` must match the
   122	current HEAD at session start. Both `orchestration/SKILL.md` and `git/SKILL.md`
   123	reference `settings.git.workflow.mode` identically (D-5 validation).
   124	
   125	**This session as N=2 witness.** Session `2026-05-24-45388fa9` (the session that
   126	authored this doc) runs in `worktree-pr` mode; its worktree lives at
   127	`.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-24-45388fa9`. Verifying
   128	that this session's writes land inside that path and that its branch name matches
   129	the regex constitutes the N=2 empirical pass of the smoke-test gate (Bundle B
   130	T1.h, `d-1-worktree-row-5-5.md` § Validation).
   131	
   132	## Lessons
   133	
   134	Lessons section is intentionally sparse as of 2026-05-24 — authored before
   135	Wrap-up ran per Bundle C DL-1 (β-1). Deepen after subsequent worktree-pr sessions
   136	per R-7.
   137	
   138	Two early observations grounded in the two sessions that have exercised the model
   139	(Bundle B ship session `2026-05-23-1b26cf20` as N=1; this session as N=2):
   140	
   141	- **The `chore` branch-type is the right choice for session branches.** The
   142	  rejected alternative `session/{date}-{ssid-short}` (iter2 of D-1) was not in
   143	  the `git/conventions.md` type registry and caused a REVISE verdict from the
   144	  Codex evaluator. The `chore` type correctly signals "housekeeping, not a product
   145	  feature" and has been in the registry from the start. Future sessions should not
   146	  re-examine the branch-type question; it is closed at D-1.
   147	- **Per-iteration commit cadence pays off on abort-recovery.** The once-at-Wrap-up
   148	  alternative was rejected at D-4 because `git worktree remove` discards
   149	  uncommitted state. In practice the per-iter cadence means each task's session
   150	  memory is committed immediately after its MEMORIZATION phase — a session aborted
   151	  mid-loop loses at most one iteration's worth of staging, not an entire session.

