   153	### P2 — Create worktree
   154	
   155	P2 is invoked from Configuration row 5.5 for worktree-first sessions (orchestration/SKILL.md Step 1), not from Execution start. The Execution-start invocation path is retired; executors are passed the existing `session.json.git.worktreePath`.
   156	
   157	Steps (run once at Configuration row 5.5 for worktree-first sessions; not re-invoked per task entering Execution):
   158	
   159	1. **Sync the base branch** — `git checkout <base-branch> && git pull --ff-only` to ensure the worktree branches from the up-to-date base.
   160	2. **Re-verify base branch on remote** — `git ls-remote --heads origin <base-branch>` (the base may have been deleted between session start and now).
   161	3. **Create the worktree** — `git worktree add -b <branch-name> .gobbi/projects/<name>/worktrees/<branch-name> <base-branch>`. Branch name follows the regex in [`conventions.md` § Branch Naming](conventions.md#branch-naming).
   162	4. **Install dependencies in the worktree** — each worktree has its own working directory; package managers, virtual environments, and build caches are not shared. Run the project's install command (e.g., `bun install`, `npm ci`) before delegating.
   163	5. **Pass the absolute worktree path** to every delegation prompt that operates on this task.
   164	
   165	### P3 — Delegate within worktree (subagent procedure)
   166	
   167	The subagent's first action is to `cd` to the worktree's absolute path. From there, the subagent follows the standard Study → Plan → Execute → Verify → Commit lifecycle (per [`execution/SKILL.md`](../execution/SKILL.md)). Per-task commit rules:
   168	
   169	- **Commit only after Verify passes** — never commit unverified work.
   170	- **One focused commit per subtask** — commit grammar per [`conventions.md` § Commit Messages](conventions.md#commit-messages).
   171	- **Commit message footer carries `AI-Provenance-Record:`** per [`conventions.md` § Commit Trailers](conventions.md#commit-trailers).
   172	- **Never push** — the manager owns push.
   173	
   174	### P4 — Push and open PR
   175	
   176	After all subtasks for the issue are complete and verified:
   177	
   178	1. `cd` to the worktree path.
   179	2. **Push the branch** — `git push -u origin <branch-name>`.
   180	3. **Open the PR** with `gh pr create` — title and body follow [`conventions.md` § Pull Request Format](conventions.md#pull-request-format).
   181	4. **Apply type label** — `gh pr edit <num> --add-label <type>` per [`conventions.md` § Label Registry](conventions.md#label-registry).
   182	5. **Monitor CI** — `gh pr checks <num> --watch` (or equivalent for external CI).
   183	
   184	### P5 — Land PR
   185	
   186	**Pre-merge gate** — all preconditions must hold before merging:
   187	
   188	- [ ] All CI checks green on the PR branch HEAD
   189	- [ ] All subtasks marked done in the plan
   190	- [ ] No subagent has uncommitted changes in the worktree
   191	- [ ] PR body has all required sections per [`conventions.md` § Pull Request Format](conventions.md#pull-request-format)
   192	- [ ] If targeting a non-default branch: note linked issues that the manager must close manually post-merge (closing keywords only trigger on default-branch merges)
   193	
   194	If any precondition fails, do not merge — surface the failing item to the user.
   195	
   196	**Merge sequence** (all preconditions pass):
   197	
   198	1. `gh pr merge <num> --squash --delete-branch` — atomic squash merge + remote branch deletion.
   199	2. `git checkout <base-branch> && git pull --ff-only` — sync the local base branch with the merge.
   200	3. Before removing the worktree: run `git status` inside it to confirm a clean working tree AND that the branch is merged into base. Then `git worktree remove .gobbi/projects/<name>/worktrees/<branch-name>`. **Never use `--force` / `-f` without explicit user approval via AskUserQuestion** — force-remove silently discards any uncommitted work inside the worktree (Forbidden Operations). If the status is unclean, commit or discard explicitly before removal.
   201	4. `git worktree prune` — clean stale references.
   202	5. **Clean up empty parent directories** — nested branch names like `feat/42-x` create `worktrees/feat/` parent dirs; `git worktree remove` only removes the leaf. Run `find .gobbi/projects/<name>/worktrees/ -type d -empty -delete`.
   203	6. **If non-default-branch PR**: close linked issues — `gh issue close <num> -c "Closed by PR #<pr-num>"` for each.
