     1	# Git Conventions
     2	
     3	Deterministic rules for branch naming, commit grammar, footer trailers, PR template, label registry, sub-issues, worktree path formula, and base branch. Every rule is expressed as a regex, a table, or a literal template so agents can self-validate before pushing.
     4	
     5	Formats align with:
     6	- [Conventional Commits v1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/) — commit grammar
     7	- [GitHub Flow](https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/quickstart/github-flow) — branch / PR lifecycle
     8	- [Linux kernel `submitting-patches.html`](https://docs.kernel.org/process/submitting-patches.html) — commit message size + voice
     9	- [`git worktree(1)`](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-worktree) — worktree semantics
    10	
    11	---
    12	
    13	## Branch Naming
    14	
    15	### Validator (two-step)
    16	
    17	Branch name validation is a two-step procedure:
    18	
    19	**Step 1 — Shape check (regex):**
    20	
    21	```regex
    22	^(feat|fix|hotfix|chore|docs|refactor|test|ci|perf|build|style)/(\d+-)?([a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*)$
    23	```
    24	
    25	The agent runs this regex against the proposed branch name before `git worktree add -b`. A mismatch is a precondition violation — surface to the user and re-derive.
    26	
    27	**Step 2 — 3-50 character length check on the description slug:**
    28	
    29	After the shape check passes, extract the description slug — everything after `<type>/` and after the optional issue number prefix (`\d+-`). Check that the slug length is between 3 and 50 characters (inclusive). A slug shorter than 3 chars is too terse to be meaningful; longer than 50 chars makes the branch name unwieldy in tooling.
    30	
    31	```
    32	description-slug = branch-name after stripping "<type>/" and optional "<issue-num>-"
    33	e.g., "feat/42-oauth-login"  → slug = "oauth-login"     (10 chars — PASS)
    34	      "feat/42-x"            → slug = "x"               (1 char  — FAIL: too short)
    35	      "feat/42-{60+ chars}"  → slug = "{60+ chars}"     (60 chars — FAIL: too long)
    36	```
    37	
    38	Both steps must pass. A branch name that passes the regex but fails the length check is still invalid.
    39	
    40	### Type prefixes
    41	
    42	| Prefix | Purpose | Example |
    43	|---|---|---|
    44	| `feat/` | New feature | `feat/42-oauth-login` |
    45	| `fix/` | Bug fix | `fix/123-null-pointer` |
    46	| `hotfix/` | Urgent production fix | `hotfix/critical-auth-leak` |
    47	| `chore/` | Maintenance, dependencies | `chore/bump-bun-1.2` |
    48	| `docs/` | Documentation only | `docs/api-reference` |
    49	| `refactor/` | Code restructuring, no behavior change | `refactor/extract-logger` |
    50	| `test/` | Test additions or modifications | `test/89-edge-cases` |
    51	| `ci/` | CI / CD configuration | `ci/cache-bun-deps` |
    52	| `perf/` | Performance improvement | `perf/cache-hot-path` |
    53	| `build/` | Build system changes | `build/migrate-vite` |
