    68	
    69	## Commit Messages
    70	
    71	Conventional Commits v1.0.0 grammar with Linux-kernel-derived size limits.
    72	
    73	### Subject regex
    74	
    75	```regex
    76	^(feat|fix|hotfix|chore|docs|refactor|test|ci|perf|build|style)(\([a-z0-9-]+\))?!?: [a-z].{1,67}[^.]$
    77	```
    78	
    79	Constraints:
    80	- **Total subject length ≤ 72 chars** (Linux kernel says 70-75; we pick 72 as the round Conventional-Commits-friendly number)
    81	- **Imperative present-tense** ("add", not "added" or "adds")
    82	- **Lowercase first letter after `: `**
    83	- **No trailing period**
    84	- **Type from the same registry as branch prefixes** (`feat` / `fix` / `hotfix` / `chore` / `docs` / `refactor` / `test` / `ci` / `perf` / `build` / `style`)
    85	- **Optional scope**: lowercase + hyphen-separated noun in parens — `feat(parser):`, `fix(auth-flow):`
    86	- **Breaking change**: append `!` before the colon — `feat(auth)!: drop password fallback`. Also requires a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer.
    87	
